       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum ibuprofen dose of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum of 800 mg. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and it doesn't add much pain or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum typical dose, and it is usually given with food.\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day). This is the usual range for analgesia.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical reason. I can add that to the order note. Otherwise, tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it."
      }
